{
  "_readme": "Shared golden test vectors for compute_breakdown/verdict_for (Python, source of truth) and its Kotlin hand-port (android/.../domain/Breakdown.kt). See TESTING.md's cross-platform section and tests/test_breakdown_golden_vectors.py. Field names are snake_case, matching the /api/breakdown wire convention - the Kotlin loader maps to its own camelCase data classes. actual_lb/limit_lb are rounded whole numbers (Python parses its actualLabel/limitLabel strings back to int; Kotlin rounds its raw Double) - this tests the math, not display formatting, which each platform already tests separately. 'requires' lists capability tags a case depends on that Kotlin's current port doesn't have; Kotlin's test runner skips any case whose requires isn't fully supported today, EXCEPT live_bug_standalone_without_hitched, which is deliberately left unskipped and is expected to fail - see that case's own comment.",
